   "flags": [],
   "use": "The standard invitation and plan for a night out: kondo nomi ni ikou (let's go for a drink sometime), kyou nomi ni ikanai? Bare nomi already means alcohol. Naming the drink is fine too (osake nomi ni iku, koohii nomi ni iku), and a café break is ocha shi ni iku. Casual speech sometimes drops ni (nomi iku).",
   "notes": "A drinking party with colleagues or a club is a nomikai, and moving on to a second place afterwards is the nijikai (second round).",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "kondo, issho ni nomi ni ikou yo.",
    "ja": "今度、一緒に飲みに行こうよ。",
    "english": "Let's go for a drink together sometime."
   },
   "examplePolite": {
    "romaji": "kondo, issho ni nomi ni ikimashou.",
    "ja": "今度、一緒に飲みに行きましょう。",
    "english": "Let's go for a drink together sometime."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "c-tabako-o-suu",
   "romaji": "tabako o suu",
   "polite": "tabako o suimasu",
   "english": "smoke (a cigarette)",
   "ja": "タバコを吸う",
   "kana": "タバコをすう",
